{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1207968-transition-from-mortal-to-changeling","id":1207968,"title":"Transition from Mortal to Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-17T06:55:05-07:00","id":1207968,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Transition from Mortal to Changeling","content":"My group is currently playing a Mortal campaign we started a while back with the idea of transitioning to a Changeling (2e if that matters) at a later date. We change off GMing periodically and it looks like my turn in the barrel is going to coincide with us transitioning to changeling.<br /> <br /> Do you have any advice an adding the Changeling template mid campaign?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3182-thinkmilitant","name":"ThinkMilitant","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T10:53:32-07:00","id":1208066,"title":"","content":"Are you going to RP the Durance? Or do a time-skip to after they've all escaped, leaving the actual Durance vague (and revealed through dialog references and flashbacks)? Same True Fae Keeper, or different ones?<br /> <br /> Other options include:<ul><li>The PCs were Fetches all along! The &quot;transition to Changeling&quot; is them finding their Changelings, then &quot;merging&quot; with them. PCs remain in control, but they can use the &quot;change&quot; in character as an excuse to rewrite certain behavioral trends, if they want.</li> <li>Use the murky &quot;What happens when a mortal replaces a Goblin Queen, then gets free themselves&quot; area. Might not be available in your setting (I think you need to have a &quot;child&quot; take the GQ's place).</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:38:39-07:00","id":1208148,"title":"","content":"Great questions! I knew I was short on information, but wasn't quite sure what would be relevant and what would just be me rambling.<br /> <br /> I was planning on lightly narrating the Durance. I fell like, at least with my group, bringing actual gameplay into it would cheapen it. Probably give them a vague taste of it up front, get them into the action, and then let extra details come out from time to time in play in flashbacks and revelations.<br /> <br /> I feel it should be the same keeper so they can conduct something of a group jail break. The group is a little weak on internal bonds and I think having that shared enemy/experience will help them explain why they stick together beyond simply being &quot;adventure buddies&quot;.<br /> <br /> How about mechanics? Any pitfalls to look out for when applying the changeling template later into a characters life like this? I presume they would get certain social merits refunded (status, resources, etc) as their fetches now have them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3182-thinkmilitant","name":"ThinkMilitant","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T14:02:57-07:00","id":1208164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThinkMilitant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1207968-transition-from-mortal-to-changeling?p=1208148#post1208148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great questions! I knew I was short on information, but wasn't quite sure what would be relevant and what would just be me rambling.<br /> <br /> I was planning on lightly narrating the Durance. I fell like, at least with my group, bringing actual gameplay into it would cheapen it. Probably give them a vague taste of it up front, get them into the action, and then let extra details come out from time to time in play in flashbacks and revelations.<br /> <br /> I feel it should be the same keeper so they can conduct something of a group jail break. The group is a little weak on internal bonds and I think having that shared enemy/experience will help them explain why they stick together beyond simply being &quot;adventure buddies&quot;.<br /> <br /> How about mechanics? Any pitfalls to look out for when applying the changeling template later into a characters life like this? I presume they would get certain social merits refunded (status, resources, etc) as their fetches now have them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ask them what they might like to keep or drop, actually. Giant is normally a &quot;character creation only&quot; merit, but becoming an Ogre is drastic enough they might want to pick that up. Or losing certain physical or mental merits and skills to reflect atrophy and refocus during the Durance.<br /> <br /> Before you start, ask them what really ties them to the world, and why they might return. Get 2-3 ideas per player, ideally. At least one will be what they return for, and the others you can keep, change (to reflect the contrast of Before and After), or eliminate them (as a Player Punch reflecting the PCs old life is over).<br /> <br /> Who is going to try to replace their Fetch, who is going to try to reconcile/team-up with their Fetch, who is going to leave their Fetch to their old life, and who is missing a Fetch (and instead might risk &quot;But you died!?&quot;)?<br /> <br /> Will anyone close to them become Fae-Touched?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T08:29:37-07:00","id":1208885,"title":"","content":"To build on <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>'s excellent foundation: this is really a moment for everyone to spend together answering questions. Ideally as a group, because players are together at the table and it will help them form bonds that reflect in some respect the bonds of suffering and support their characters have passed through. Even if that passage is &quot;behind the curtain&quot;, so to speak.<br /> <br /> Ask them which skills or attributes were key to their escape. Have them each pick three (three skills, three attributes). As you define their actual escape and reveal it in flashback sessions, you can call for each player to use these in combinations for a powerful reminder. Optionally, if you think it is relevant, you might let a player substitute a Merit for either an attribute or skill.<br /> <br /> Do they know what their Seemings will be? Kith? How that has affected their appearance? <br /> <br /> If not, then you might ask them to point to three skills and three attributes as well that defined their Durance. Merit substitution again (&quot;I was a tall pillar holding things up, so huge size was kinda important.&quot;) That could help you suggest their characteristics.<br /> <br /> If you want to be real daring, and you have the right group, after playing questions have them each pass their sheet to the player on the right, to fill out Kith and Seeming. This would effectively reinforce the lack of agency in the Durance, but it's not for everyone! (I did this once for an Aberrant game back in the day.)<br /> <br /> In contrast, you will want to define your courts fairly well--at least the key attributes and approaches of the main persons there, since once the PCs get back giving them agency to choose their court is, along with the question of fetches, a key empowerment point.<br /> <br /> The actual abduction/seduction sequence you can also include in a flashback, showing how the group as a whole reacted or something to land in their trap. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf (who has actually not run CtL, yet...)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T15:33:40-07:00","id":1211185,"title":"","content":"Equinox Road actually has a section(and mechanical progression) for this subject in Chapter 3. Check it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}